  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "TAN reduces arguments with x87 FPREM1(x, FLDPI/2) and rejects |x| >= 2^27 with #NUM!, drifting at large inputs",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, TAN(x) rejects |x| >= 2^27 (134,217,728) with #NUM! and otherwise evaluates FPREM1(x, FLDPI/2), FPTAN, and -1/tan(r) in extended precision on odd quadrants before a single store to binary64. Because reduction uses the 64-bit x87 FLDPI/2 constant rather than exact pi/2, large arguments drift from mathematical tan(x): TAN(81343728.62285979) differs from exact tan(x) by ~1.20e7 ULPs.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 2,114/2,114 full-bank and 120/120 pinned TAN rows.",
